  "response": "Here are the short-answer quiz questions in JSON format:\n\n[\n  {\n    \"q\": \"What is the principle behind piezoelectric crystals?\",\n    \"a\": \"Piezoelectric crystals generate charge when mechanically stressed.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"q\": \"What is the working principle of accelerometers?\",\n    \"a\": \"Vibration causes mass to compress crystal, generating charge proportional to acceleration.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"q\": \"What is strain measurement defined as?\",\n    \"a\": \"Strain is defined as ΔL/L (change in length divided by original length).\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"q\": \"What is a reflex gauge?\",\n    \"a\": \"A type of gauge that uses prism glass, with liquid appearing dark and vapor appearing bright.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"q\": \"How does Archimedes' principle apply to level measurement?\",\n    \"a\": \"Increase in liquid level increases buoyant force on displacer.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"q\": \"What is the principle behind capacitive level sensors?\",\n    \"a\": \"Change in dielectric changes capacitance.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"q\": \"What is charge sensitivity defined as?\",\n    \"a\": \"Change in charge per unit displacement (less used but theoretically present).\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"q\": \"What are the advantages of LVDTs?\",\n    \"a\": \"High output signal, simple and low cost, good linearity, and easy to interface.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"q\": \"How do RTDs work?\",\n    \"a\": \"By measuring resistance change due to temperature changes (Seebeck Effect).\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"q\": \"What is the difference between 2-wire, 3-wire, and 4-wire RTD configurations?\",\n    \"a\": \"2-wire: simplest, but lowest accuracy; 3-wire: most common, good accuracy; 4-wire: best accuracy.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"q\": \"What is the principle behind thermocouples?\",\n    \"a\": \"Based on Seebeck Effect: EMF produced proportional to temperature difference between dissimilar metals.\"\n  }\n]",
